    {
      "ordinal": 11,
      "depth": 2,
      "kind": "rule",
      "number": "2.1.2",
      "title": "Serious Issue",
      "body": "● A serious issue is a rule violation that damages the reputation of the Committee or Buhurt International. However, this does not necessarily mean that the Committee member can no longer collaborate with the organization.\n● It's an issue severe enough to erode the Council's confidence in the Authenticity Committee member. A three-month suspension is intended to indicate that this behavior is not compliant with the Authenticity Committee's rules.\nExamples of serious issues:\n●Extremely inappropriate public behavior (including online). I.e: insulting a third party, ●Showing bias during armor and weapons checks at a Buhurt International tournament or event, ●Multiple misapplications of rules during more than one event.",
      "page_from": 4,
      "page_to": 4,
