      "number": "2.1.3",
      "title": "Major Issue",
      "body": "A major issue is a rule violation that severely damages the reputation of the Committee or Buhurt International. This level of breach indicates that it is no longer possible to continue collaborating with the Committee member.\nIt’s an issue severe enough to warrant ending the collaboration, as it signifies a compromise to the integrity of the Committee, making further cooperation impossible.\nExamples of major issues :\n●Unacceptable public behavior. I.e: aggressing a third party, ●Multiple sanctions for minor and serious issues.",
